Saturate the end position in ff_jpegxl_collect_codestream_header() instead of letting it wrap.

pos is an int64_t, and a box with a 64-bit size (size == 1) adds an attacker-chosen uint64_t
to it. FFMIN(pos, INT_MAX) then returns a negative or wrapped value that is truncated to int,
e.g. 0 for a jxlp box of size 0xbd000000ffffffef after 21 bytes of boxes. jpegxl_parse() uses
the result as the end of the image (ctx->next), emits a zero-length frame and consumes nothing,
and parse_packet() (libavformat/demux.c) calls the parser again with the same data forever:
ffprobe hangs on a 49-byte file. Clamp pos to INT_MAX, which the parser already treats as
"the image continues past this buffer".
Includes the FATE test fate-jpegxl-parse (libavcodec/tests/jpegxl_parse.c).
Not fixed upstream as of 224205649a; the related 47605bb2cd (ffmpeg PR 25511) fixed special
box sizes in skip_boxes() only.

diff --git a/libavcodec/Makefile b/libavcodec/Makefile
index f12ad9c..4757093 100644
--- a/libavcodec/Makefile
+++ b/libavcodec/Makefile
@@ -1402,6 +1402,7 @@ TESTPROGS-$(CONFIG_CELP_MATH)             += celp_math
 TESTPROGS-$(CONFIG_ENCODERS)              += hw_base_encode
 TESTPROGS-$(CONFIG_GOLOMB)                += golomb
 TESTPROGS-$(CONFIG_IDCTDSP)               += dct
+TESTPROGS-$(CONFIG_JPEGXL_PARSER)         += jpegxl_parse
 TESTPROGS-$(CONFIG_DXV_ENCODER)           += hashtable
 TESTPROGS-$(CONFIG_MJPEG_ENCODER)         += mjpegenc_huffman
 TESTPROGS-$(CONFIG_MPEGAUDIOHEADER)       += mpegaudiodecheader
diff --git a/libavcodec/jpegxl_parse.c b/libavcodec/jpegxl_parse.c
index 47b831e..5888042 100644
--- a/libavcodec/jpegxl_parse.c
+++ b/libavcodec/jpegxl_parse.c
@@ -502,6 +502,8 @@ int ff_jpegxl_collect_codestream_header(const uint8_t *input_buffer, int input_l
          */
         if (!size)
             size = bytestream2_get_bytes_left(&gb);
+        else if (size > INT_MAX - head_size - pos)
+            pos = INT_MAX; /* the box ends beyond anything we can index */
         else
             pos += size + head_size;
 
diff --git a/libavcodec/tests/jpegxl_parse.c b/libavcodec/tests/jpegxl_parse.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..52aecee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libavcodec/tests/jpegxl_parse.c
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
